---
import media from '../data/project-media.json';
import ProjectImage from './ProjectImage.astro';

const sizes =
  '(max-width: 600px) min(430px, 100vw - 40px), (max-width: 1000px) 44vw, 430px';
---

<article class="project" id="hairnow" aria-labelledby="hairnow-title">
  <div class="project-top">
    <span class="mono">03 / MOBILE & FULL-STACK ENGINEERING</span>
    <span class="project-status">Team project</span>
  </div>
  <div class="project-intro">
    <h3 id="hairnow-title">HairNow</h3>
    <div>
      <h4>From the service menu to the stylist’s inbox.</h4>
      <p>
        In HairNow, customers choose a service, a stylist and a time. The
        stylist can then confirm or decline the request. I built the overlap
        check and added role switching to the demo so you can try the customer,
        employee and salon owner views in one workspace.
      </p>
      <a class="inline-link" href="https://hairnow-demo.web.app/">
        Try the HairNow demo <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="hairnow-views">
    <ProjectImage
      image={media['hairnow-services']}
      alt="HairNow’s service menu lists a 20-minute Beard Trim and a 45-minute Classic Cut."
      label="CUSTOMER / CHOOSE A SERVICE"
      caption="The service determines how much time to reserve with the stylist."
      sizes={sizes}
    />
    <div>
      <ProjectImage
        image={media['hairnow-request']}
        alt="The employee inbox shows a Classic Cut from 11:00 to 11:45 with Confirm and Decline controls."
        label="EMPLOYEE / REVIEW A REQUEST"
        caption="A sample Classic Cut arrives in the inbox with its start and end time."
        sizes={sizes}
      />
      <div class="engineering-note">
        <h5>When two requests overlap</h5>
        <p>
          An 11:30 trim would overlap that 11:00 cut. My booking logic checks a
          temporary lock for each minute of the stylist’s time. If the interval
          is free, one Firestore transaction writes the locks and the
          appointment request together.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="project-colophon">
    <p>Flutter / Dart / Firebase Authentication / Cloud Firestore</p>
    <p>Live demo captures · Sample booking data</p>
  </div>
</article>

<style>
  .hairnow-views {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 430px));
    justify-content: center;
    gap: clamp(24px, 6vw, 80px);
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }
  .engineering-note h5 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .engineering-note p {
    line-height: 1.75;
  }
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .hairnow-views {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 430px);
      gap: 28px;
    }
  }
</style>
